From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: SplitView

WinUI 2's NavigationView is built on a SplitView (RootSplitView); without one, Windows Terminal's settings page showed nothing below its top bar. Ours lays out its Pane beside its Content (Inline, CompactInline) or over it (Overlay, CompactOverlay), OpenPaneLength wide when open and CompactPaneLength when closed in the compact modes, mirrored for PanePlacement Right, with PaneBackground under the pane. Opening and closing raise PaneOpening and PaneOpened, PaneClosing (which may cancel) and PaneClosed. TemplateSettings gives the lengths. The markup takes its DisplayMode, PanePlacement and LightDismissOverlayMode names.
